{
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  // 2026-11-18 - GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf (picomatch ReDoS through single-branch
  // repeated extglobs) was allowlisted here while it was live and unfixable:
  // no patched picomatch release exists (latest 4.0.7, advisory range
  // <=4.0.7, first_patched_version null) and the advisory update on
  // 2026-11-17 turned previously green main red.  Every lockfile path was
  // build- or test-time tooling running the project's own static glob
  // patterns, never attacker-controlled input: vitest/vite/tinyglobby (test),
  // typescript-eslint and eslint-config-next/fast-glob (lint), and
  // @sentry/nextjs sourcemap-upload bundler plugins (build).  GitHub withdrew
  // the advisory on 2026-11-18 (withdrawn_at 2026-11-18T15:38:56Z, withdrawn
  // because it is not a security issue), so npm no longer reports it and the
  // entry was dropped on 2026-11-22 under the same policy as the braces entry
  // below.
  //
  // 2026-11-18 - dropped the 2026-10-05 braces entry (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm).
  // That advisory is withdrawn (GitHub advisory title: "Withdrawn Advisory:
  // braces vulnerable to stack-exhaustion denial of service..."; no
  // firstPatchedVersion).  audit-ci no longer matches it, even though
  // braces 3.0.3 remains in the lockfile.  A stale allowlist entry would
  // silently suppress a future braces advisory if this GHSA were reused
  // or reopened.  Re-review if the advisory is republished.
  //
  // 2026-11-22 (MM) - the allowlist is empty on purpose.  Every id it held
  // was a withdrawn advisory, and a retained withdrawn id would suppress a
  // real republished advisory under the same GHSA, which is the failure the
  // braces entry above cites.  npm audit reports 0 high advisories at this
  // tree, so the gate passes at high severity with no suppression and a
  // republished advisory turns main red instead of passing silently.
  // Re-review if npm reports a high or critical advisory whose affected range
  // has no patched release and whose affected paths never see
  // attacker-controlled input.
  "high": true,
  "allowlist": []
}
